{%- comment -%} Styles live in assets/ha-sections.css, loaded once in layout/theme.liquid. {%- endcomment -%}

{%- comment -%}
  Hartwick Atelier — THE CIRCLE, a row of numbered columns.

  One section, used twice on the Circle page, because the design asks the same
  question twice in the same shape:

      WHAT THE CIRCLE HOLDS   01 Early viewing · 02 Private appointments ·
                              03 Atelier notes · 04 Care and repair
      HOW IT WORKS            01 Request · 02 Reply · 03 Access

  A heading on the left, an optional paragraph set against it on the right, then
  a rule-separated row of numbered columns beneath. Two, three or four columns —
  the grid counts the blocks rather than being told, so adding a fifth is a
  block, not a rebuild.

  Nothing here is Circle-specific in the code. It is a general editorial row and
  can be used on any page.

  Journey layout (About-page wireframe, 15 September 2026):

      A JOURNEY INTO THE HOUSE            heading in the identify voice
      01              02                  a serif numeral over its own rule,
      ────────        ────────            then the column heading in small
      COSTUME +       IMAGE +             capitals, then a paragraph in the
      CULTURE         PLACE               record voice
      An early …      Documentary …

  Same blocks, same settings; `layout` switches the dressing, so the About
  page and the Circle page share one section rather than two near-copies.

  ⚠️ ALL COPY IS PLACEHOLDER. Per CLAUDE.md nothing about the Circle — what it
  offers, how someone is considered, what a member receives — may be written by
  us. Every default below is marked and the section carries the standard
  provisional notice until Aloha supplies the real wording.
{%- endcomment -%}

<section class="ha-section ha-ccols ha-ccols--{{ section.settings.layout | default: 'circle' }}{% unless section.settings.field == 'page' or section.settings.field == blank %} ha-section--field-{{ section.settings.field }}{% endunless %}">
  <div class="ha-wrap">

    <div class="ha-ccols__head">
      <div class="ha-ccols__head-lead">
        {%- if section.settings.eyebrow != blank -%}
          <p class="ha-eyebrow ha-record">{{ section.settings.eyebrow }}</p>
        {%- endif -%}
        {%- if section.settings.heading != blank -%}
          {%- if section.settings.layout == 'journey' -%}
            <h2 class="ha-ccols__heading ha-ccols__heading--identify ha-narrate">{{ section.settings.heading }}</h2>
          {%- else -%}
            <h2 class="ha-display ha-narrate ha-ccols__heading">{{ section.settings.heading }}</h2>
          {%- endif -%}
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>

      {%- comment -%}
        The paragraph sits opposite the heading rather than under it — the
        design sets them as two voices in conversation across the page, not as
        a heading and its own subtitle.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- if section.settings.aside != blank -%}
        <div class="ha-ccols__aside ha-body ha-narrate">{{ section.settings.aside }}</div>
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>

    {%- if section.blocks.size > 0 -%}
      <ol class="ha-ccols__row ha-ccols__row--{{ section.blocks.size }}" role="list">
        {%- for block in section.blocks -%}
          <li class="ha-ccols__col" {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
            {%- if section.settings.layout == 'journey' -%}
              <p class="ha-ccols__num ha-narrate" aria-hidden="true">{{ forloop.index | prepend: '0' | slice: -2, 2 }}</p>
              {%- if block.settings.heading != blank -%}
                <h3 class="ha-ccols__col-heading ha-ccols__col-heading--identify ha-narrate">{{ block.settings.heading }}</h3>
              {%- endif -%}
              {%- if block.settings.body != blank -%}
                <div class="ha-ccols__body ha-record ha-record--prose">{{ block.settings.body }}</div>
              {%- endif -%}
            {%- else -%}
            {%- comment -%}
              The number is decorative — a reader hearing this list already
              knows it is the third of four from the list semantics, and having
              "zero three" read aloud before every heading is noise. The label
              beside it is not decorative and stays announced.
            {%- endcomment -%}
            <p class="ha-ccols__mark ha-record">
              <span aria-hidden="true">{{ forloop.index | prepend: '0' | slice: -2, 2 }}</span>
              {%- comment -%}
                The design writes this rank as "01 / REQUEST". The slash is
                punctuation between two things a sighted reader takes in at
                once; read aloud it is noise, so it is hidden along with the
                number while the word itself stays announced. Where a column
                has no word — the four on "What the Circle holds" — neither the
                slash nor the empty span is printed at all.
              {%- endcomment -%}
              {%- if block.settings.label != blank -%}
                <span class="ha-ccols__slash" aria-hidden="true">/</span>
                <span class="ha-ccols__label">{{ block.settings.label }}</span>
              {%- endif -%}
            </p>

            {%- if block.settings.heading != blank -%}
              <h3 class="ha-ccols__col-heading ha-narrate">{{ block.settings.heading }}</h3>
            {%- endif -%}

            {%- if block.settings.body != blank -%}
              <div class="ha-ccols__body ha-narrate">{{ block.settings.body }}</div>
            {%- endif -%}
            {%- endif -%}
          </li>
        {%- endfor -%}
      </ol>
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- render 'ha-placeholder-note', show: section.settings.show_placeholder_note -%}
  </div>
</section>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "HA — Numbered columns",
  "tag": "section",
  "class": "ha-section-wrapper",
  "max_blocks": 6,
  "settings": [
    { "type": "select", "id": "layout", "label": "Layout", "default": "circle", "options": [
      { "value": "circle", "label": "Rules between columns (The Circle)" },
      { "value": "journey", "label": "Numeral over a rule, record body (About)" }
    ] },
    { "type": "select", "id": "field", "label": "Field colour", "default": "page", "options": [
      { "value": "page", "label": "Page ground" },
      { "value": "sand", "label": "Sand (one step darker)" },
      { "value": "white", "label": "White" },
      { "value": "peat", "label": "Peat (dark)" },
      { "value": "clay", "label": "Clay" },
      { "value": "botanical", "label": "Botanical" },
      { "value": "slate", "label": "Slate (dark)" }
    ] },
    { "type": "text", "id": "eyebrow", "label": "Eyebrow" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "heading", "label": "Heading" },
    { "type": "richtext", "id": "aside", "label": "Paragraph opposite the heading" },
    {
      "type": "header", "content": "Provisional content",
      "info": "Leave the notice on until Aloha has supplied the final wording. Nothing about The Circle may be written by the build."
    },
    { "type": "checkbox", "id": "show_placeholder_note", "label": "Show placeholder notice", "default": true }
  ],
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "column",
      "name": "Column",
      "settings": [
        { "type": "text", "id": "label", "label": "Label", "info": "Printed after the rank as \"01 / REQUEST\". Leave empty for a bare number." },
        { "type": "text", "id": "heading", "label": "Heading" },
        { "type": "richtext", "id": "body", "label": "Body" }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "presets": [{ "name": "Hartwick — Numbered columns" }]
}
{% endschema %}
